# Query Keys & Caching

All query keys are defined in `@/lib/query-keys.ts`. Never hardcode key arrays.

## Key Structure

```typescript
import { queryKeys } from "@/lib/query-keys"

queryKeys.product.all                    // ["product"]
queryKeys.product.bySlug("ml-daily-klatch")
queryKeys.cart.all                       // ["cart"]
queryKeys.order.byId(id)
```

Use a **singular** prefix for one resource (`"product"`). Use a **plural** prefix only for list/table queries if you add them later.

## StaleTime Constants

```typescript
import { STALE_TIME } from "@/lib/query-keys"

STALE_TIME.REALTIME      // 30s — cart, live stock
STALE_TIME.SEMI_STATIC   // 5min — product details
STALE_TIME.STATIC        // Infinity — static options
```

## Invalidation After Mutation

**Default: `invalidateQueries`.** It marks matching queries stale and refetches **active** ones automatically. Inactive cache entries refresh the next time something subscribes.

```typescript
await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: queryKeys.cart.all })
```

**Use `refetchQueries`** only when you **must** force an immediate network refetch. Otherwise keep **`invalidateQueries`**.

## Adding New Query Keys

Add to `queryKeys` in `query-keys.ts`. Follow the existing pattern: `all` (prefix), `byId` / `bySlug`, then more specific keys.
